dit/081: happyyzy's llama.cpp PR #28446 ("opencl: fuse QK normalization and RoPE", open, MIT), rebased onto our ggml
after 067 + 080: a DiT block's QKV split, Q/K norms and RoPE before each attention as one preprocessing kernel. Its
table on the Adreno 830: Klein 4B 1024^2 4 steps 37.65 -> 21.15 s/step; we measured 37-47 without it (2026-10-31).
Our changes: the kernel added to our CMake list (it held qknorm_rope too), and 080's yield log reset/printed only by
the outermost graph_compute (the fusion computes sub-graphs through it), GGML_OPENCL_NO_QKNORM_ROPE=1 to decline our own
fused Q/K norm + RoPE (the PR matches only RMS_NORM + ROPE, which our sd.cpp never builds while that op is taken), and
one log line when the fusion fires.
Text before the first diff line is ignored by git apply.

